 'Platform clocks should be kept in good order, and their hands must not be stopped or tampered with. The clocks must be wound up each night and must be tested daily by the station master or other authorized officer. Any damage or deterioration in the working of a platform clock must be reported immediately to the district engineer.' [more]
Railway stations have been crucial hubs of human activity since the early days of rail travel. From ticket offices to waiting rooms, restaurants to restrooms, these stations have played a vital role in connecting communities across the globe. The railway station is more than just a stop on the way to our destination; it is a place where lives are changed, connections are made and memories are forged. In this blog, we'll explore the story of railway stations and how they have evolved over time. From historic buildings to modern architectural marvels, we'll examine the role of these structures in shaping the modern world. We'll also delve into the stories of people who have passed through these stations, sharing their stories and experiences. Join us on this journey as we explore the world of railway stations! [less]
A railway station is a place where people come together – a place where lives intersect. It's a spot where stories are shared, and memories are made. Whether you're a traveler, a resident, or a historian, a railway station is an integral part of your journey. As we explore the evolution of railway stations, we'll take you on a trip around the world, sharing stories of iconic stations, and the people who make them tick. From the iconic Grand Central Terminal in New York to the bustling Gare du Nord in Paris, each railway station has a unique story to tell. [more]
